    {
      "test_id": "chat-065",
      "timestamp": "2026-08-31T13:12:07.975287+00:00",
      "question": "Explain in detail the CRI missions, investor support, sectors, procedures and regional indicators.",
      "language": "en",
      "category": "token_stress",
      "status": "answered",
      "answer": "The CRI TTA (Regional Investment Center of Tangier - Tetouan - Al Hoceima) has a mission to provide economic incentives and promote the region's investment offers. It compiles a database of 50 turnkey investment projects, organized by sector and territory, to highlight the region's strengths and opportunities. The identification of these projects involves four main components: import substitution, meeting national and global demand, integrating value chains, and collective reflection with local players. The CRI provides various support services, including local workspace, IT infrastructure, coaching and assistance services (legal, accounting, banking), strategic services (marketing, financial advice, intellectual property, market research), access to a network of investment funds and partners, and qualified personnel. Investors' expectations regarding the CRI include strengthening support for companies (9%), assistance in finding land solutions (6%), and finding financial/subsidy solutions (6%). The CRI TTA also has a platform called MANAR AL MOUSTATMIR, which is a virtual one-stop shop for investor and project owner support. The CRI TTA's regional indicators are assessed through a survey that covers investors' perception of the business climate, satisfaction with CRI services, and stakeholders' perspectives on the business climate, including environmental and energy efficiency matters.",
